From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:23:28 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wgengine/router/osrouter: distinguish local and peer routes
 on Windows

Windows installs a host route for each assigned address. Skip only
exact local hosts when building routes so a subnet whose base is an
assigned address still reaches its peers.

Use the installed route's protocol to distinguish local host and
connected routes from static peer routes, including a host at the last
address in a routed subnet. Windows reports an assigned next hop as
unspecified. Use that form so the next sync recognizes the route.

Change-Id: I94ad1e43096b8fb03e592f84313181091e5d1858
Signed-off-by: Brody Franks <brody@franks.id.au>
